---
description: Concise code, no dead code, and test coverage standards
alwaysApply: true
---

# Writing Code

- Write concise, minimal code. Prefer fewer lines over verbose implementations.
- Prefer small, single-responsibility components.
- Never leave dead code, commented-out code, unused variables/imports/functions, or unreachable code.
- Write tests for all code. Tests live in same folder as components. Aim for > 75% test coverage. Flag all changes made to existing tests.
- Always ensure code passes lint and format requirments. After making any code changes, always run: npm run format -- --write .

# Reviewing Code

- Suggest removing over-engineered abstractions that aren't actively used.
- Check if code will break under unexpected input.
